 ### [CPU Fallback Sort Path](5586-cpu-fallback-sort-path.md)
-This strategy explicitly executes sorting on the CPU when GPU compute shaders are unavailable, disabled, or insufficient, allowing the GPU to focus solely on rasterization [5586-cpu-fallback-sort-path.md]. It differs from GPU-based sorting (like bitonic sort) by avoiding the overhead of complex GPU sorting kernels and relying on CPU-side algorithms (radix or $O(n \log n)$). It is chosen for compatibility with older hardware or web environments where WebGPU compute is not supported.
