 ### WASM/SIMD CPU Splat Sorting
-An optimization of the CPU sort path implemented in C++ using WebAssembly (WASM) SIMD instructions to accelerate the sorting process [S3, unofficial]. It differs from generic CPU sorting by leveraging vectorized instructions for parallel comparison and swapping. It includes parameters `integerBasedSort` (to force floating-point sorting for large scenes) and `splatSortDistanceMapPrecision` [S3, unofficial]. It is chosen for web-based viewers requiring better performance than standard JS sorting while maintaining GPU offloading for rendering.
